---
const outcomes = [
  { dot: "var(--color-status-pass)", name: "PassThrough", body: "Not an agent and no key — no record, gone." },
  { dot: "var(--color-status-grant)", name: "Granted", body: "Within the policy — a lease token, immediately." },
  { dot: "var(--color-status-queue)", name: "Queued", body: "Over the limit — a poll token instead of silence." },
  {
    dot: "var(--color-status-bill)",
    name: "BillWalled",
    body: "A fourth lane, wired to a real HTTP 402 in the controller — the status code fires the moment the service can produce it; no capacity rule or payment processor decides that yet.",
  },
];
---

<div id="sequence" class="border-b border-rule">
  <div class="section" style="max-width: 1120px; padding-top: 96px; padding-bottom: 72px;">
    <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
    <h2
      class="mt-5 font-bold tracking-tight text-ink"
      style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4.4vw, 46px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.04em;"
    >
      What happens to one request
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[600px] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Not a pipeline diagram — this is the actual sequence, in the order it runs.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 gap-x-12 border-t border-rule py-9">
        <div class="max-w-full flex-[0_0_300px]">
          <div class="mono text-[13px] font-medium text-neutral">1.0</div>
          <div class="mt-2.5 text-[32px] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">Evaluate.</div>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 min-w-0 flex-[1_1_420px] text-base leading-[1.7] text-ink-3">
          The sidecar calls bufferq before the backend does any work — route, tenant, the
          caller's User-Agent and IP, and an API key + policy if one was presented.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 gap-x-12 border-t border-rule py-9">
        <div class="max-w-full flex-[0_0_300px]">
          <div class="mono text-[13px] font-medium text-neutral">2.0</div>
          <div class="mt-2.5 text-[32px] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">Classify.</div>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 min-w-0 flex-[1_1_420px] text-base leading-[1.7] text-ink-3">
          No key: bufferq classifies the caller — Agent, StandardApi, Human, or Unknown — from
          request signals. A key: its rate-limit policy takes over instead.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 gap-x-12 border-t border-rule py-9">
        <div class="max-w-full flex-[0_0_300px]">
          <div class="mono text-[13px] font-medium text-neutral">3.0</div>
          <div class="mt-2.5 text-[32px] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">Decide.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="min-w-0 flex-[1_1_420px]">
          {
            outcomes.map((o, i) => (
              <div
                class={`flex flex-wrap gap-2 gap-x-6 py-4 ${i === 0 ? "pb-4 pt-0" : "border-t"}`}
                style={i === 0 ? undefined : "border-color: var(--color-rule-2);"}
              >
                <div class="mono flex flex-[0_0_150px] items-center gap-2.5 text-[13px] font-medium leading-5">
                  <span aria-hidden="true" class="block h-[9px] w-[9px] rounded-full" style={`background:${o.dot}`} />
                  {o.name}
                </div>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-[1_1_260px] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-3">{o.body}</div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 gap-x-12 border-t border-rule py-9">
        <div class="max-w-full flex-[0_0_300px]">
          <div class="mono text-[13px] font-medium text-neutral">4.0</div>
          <div class="mt-2.5 text-[32px] font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-ink">Poll.</div>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 min-w-0 flex-[1_1_420px] text-base leading-[1.7] text-ink-3">
          Only reachable from Queued. The caller asks "can I come in now?" bufferq re-checks the
          same window and either mints a real lease or says wait — and the response carries a
          links object naming the next request (poll again, or complete), so the caller doesn't
          have to hardcode routes to find out.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
